.TH tuquadrant n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuquadrant
.PP
A Mermaid\-style \fBquadrant chart\fR renderer for the \fBtuflow\fR diagram family. It parses a Mermaid \fBquadrantChart\fR block into a small model and renders it to SVG or PNG with the pure\-Tcl drawing backends (\fBtclutils::tusvg\fR / \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR). No Tk, no browser, no external rasteriser.
.PP
A quadrant chart is not a node\-edge graph, so \fBtuquadrant\fR does \fBnot\fR go through \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR; it owns its own parse and draw step, exposing the same \fBtoSvg\fR / \fBtoPng\fR shape the other renderers use. That lets the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade treat every diagram family uniformly: \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR detect a \fBquadrantChart\fR block and dispatch here (like \fBpie\fR and \fBxychart\-beta\fR).
.PP
The plot is a unit square split into four tinted quadrants; data points are placed at their normalised \fB0..1\fR coordinates with the same routine on both backends, so the SVG and the raster output stay congruent.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuquadrant 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuquadrant::parse    text                       ;# -> model dict
::tclutils::tuquadrant::toSvg    model ?-opt val ...?        ;# -> SVG string
::tclutils::tuquadrant::toPng    model ?-opt val ...?        ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tuquadrant::writeSvg model file ?-opt val ...?   ;# -> file (SVG)
::tclutils::tuquadrant::writePng model file ?-opt val ...?   ;# -> file (PNG)
.CE
.PP
\fBparse\fR turns Mermaid \fBquadrantChart\fR source into a model dict with keys \fBtitle\fR, \fBxleft\fR/\fBxright\fR, \fBybottom\fR/\fBytop\fR, \fBq1\fR..\fBq4\fR (quadrant labels) and \fBpoints\fR (a list of \fB{name x y}\fR with \fBx\fR,\fBy\fR in \fB0..1\fR). The render commands take that model.
.PP
Render options (all optional):
.CS
-width  N      chart width in logical px           (default 420)
-height N      chart height in logical px          (default 420)
-scale  N      raster scale, positive integer      (default 1; toPng only)
-fontfile F    real TTF/OTF for labels (raster)    (default: 6x8 bitmap font)
.CE
.PP
The SVG backend ignores \fB\-scale\fR and \fB\-fontfile\fR (it uses a fixed \fBmonospace\fR viewer font locked to the 6x8 metric). On the raster backend \fB\-scale N\fR multiplies the pixel dimensions and the font scale by \fBN\fR.
.SS "Input grammar (Mermaid \fBquadrantChart\fR subset)"
.CS
quadrantChart                      %% header
title <text>                       %% chart title
x-axis <left> --> <right>          %% x-axis end labels (axis is 0..1)
y-axis <bottom> --> <top>          %% y-axis end labels (axis is 0..1)
quadrant-1 <text> ... quadrant-4   %% 1=top-right, 2=top-left,
                                   %% 3=bottom-left, 4=bottom-right
<Point Name>: [x, y]               %% point at normalised 0..1 coords
%% ...                             %% comment, ignored
.CE
.PP
Any of title, axes, quadrant labels or points counts as content; a completely empty source is an error. A trailing style hint after a point (\fBradius:\fR, \fBcolor:\fR, ...) is accepted and ignored.
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuquadrant
namespace import ::tclutils::tuquadrant::*

set src {quadrantChart
    title Reach and engagement of campaigns
    x-axis Low Reach --> High Reach
    y-axis Low Engagement --> High Engagement
    quadrant-1 We should expand
    quadrant-2 Need to promote
    quadrant-3 Re-evaluate
    quadrant-4 May be improved
    Campaign A: [0.3, 0.6]
    Campaign B: [0.45, 0.23]
    Campaign C: [0.57, 0.69]
}

set m [parse $src]
writePng $m quad.png -scale 3
writeSvg $m quad.svg
.CE
.PP
Through the \fBtuflow\fR facade the same source renders without an explicit model:
.CS
package require tclutils::tuflow
::tclutils::tuflow::toPng $src -scale 3      ;# facade detects the quadrantChart block
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Point colours come from a fixed qualitative palette (10 entries) that cycles when there are more points than colours.
.IP \(bu
v1 limitations (honest): per\-point style hints (\fBradius:\fR, \fBcolor:\fR, ...) are ignored; the y\-axis end labels are placed horizontally in the left margin, not rotated; coordinates outside \fB0..1\fR are clamped.
.IP \(bu
Labels use the \fBtupngdraw\fR 6x8 bitmap font by default. With \fB\-fontfile\fR on the raster backend a real outline font is used via \fBfillcontours\fR (lazy \fBGlyphs\fR, unbundled); a set\-but\-missing path is a hard error, a missing \fBGlyphs\fR package degrades silently to the bitmap font.
.IP \(bu
Companion modules: \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR and \fBtclutils::tusvg\fR (backends), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (facade / dispatch), \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (the node\-edge graph renderer for the other Mermaid types).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUQUADRANT <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no content at all), \fBARG\fR (bad render option, e.g. non\-integer \fB\-scale\fR), \fBFONT\fR (a \fB\-fontfile\fR path that does not exist).
